{"title":"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CRITICAL_THINKING!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CRITICAL THINKING!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The twelve-sided figure shown has been drawn on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/5094c6dc4de7f42c8d47e35fa03c207d2cbcadee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\text{ cm}\\times 1 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"93\" height=\"12\" /> graph paper. What is the area of the figure in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb06de78ae4ef6fc2731e0abb6788477c03a7b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cm}^2$\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/d/f4d92072ddf7f5314e710dc9641eb84c3ea32879.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(8mm); for (int i=0; i&lt;7; ++i) {   draw((i,0)--(i,7),gray);   draw((0,i+1)--(7,i+1),gray); } draw((1,3)--(2,4)--(2,5)--(3,6)--(4,5)--(5,5)--(6,4)--(5,3)--(5,2)--(4,1)--(3,2)--(2,2)--cycle,black+2bp); [/asy]\" width=\"268\" height=\"268\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce513e2dcc4ebc0416b416bff2198f7a46e1decc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 12 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 12.5 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 13 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 13.5 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"427\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We count <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/0/c9047977a9bd03c451567fa47fddf838db16c91d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot 3=9$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> unit squares in the middle, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> small triangles, which gives 4 rectangles each with an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fe045738d9ab58a389648197f0482e9b7186730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9+4=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"129\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can see here that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> total squares in the middle. We also see that the triangles that make the corners of the shape have an area half the squares' area. Then, we can easily find that each corner has an area of one square and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> corners so we add that to the original 9 squares to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fe045738d9ab58a389648197f0482e9b7186730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9+4=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"129\" height=\"28\" />. That is how I did it. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can apply Pick's Theorem here. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> lattice points, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> lattice points on the boundary. Then,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/4/8d4221bda95dc3240fa56afce546af5959eeed19.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8 + 12 \\div 2 - 1 = \\boxed {\\textbf{(C) }13}.\\]\" width=\"204\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Shoelace_Theorem\" title=\"Shoelace Theorem\">Shoelace Theorem</a> and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bdcca6b76f9468214cfbf163eb86586356a4f61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~SaxStreak\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CRITICAL_THINKING.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CRITICAL_THINKING!!!)\">Video Solution (CRITICAL THINKING!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CRITICAL THINKING!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7qY99daRZUA\">https://youtu.be/7qY99daRZUA</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/huLjsiLQS90\">https://youtu.be/huLjsiLQS90</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/51K3uCzntWs?t=1338\">https://youtu.be/51K3uCzntWs?t=1338</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/